# Deadfall bough (#363, D88), native 112x24, one frame. Rope knots at x 40 and 55 (the pivot between them, 48, 9);
# the bare snag on the left ends at (8, 17); the thick right end goes into a Decor trunk: no end grain (a sawn end reads as
# cut, not grown), it swells by a row up and down into a dark bark collar open at the frame's edge (D122). Mirrored for swing=right.
# Joint (D130, 2026-11-24): the collar at the right edge is the trunk's red-brown bark (1 2 4) and the root (columns 104-111)
# ramps into it through w and a half step 6; keys 1, 2, 4, 6 are kept out of the moon rim.
